// CV: Acid Bass — ADSR filter envelope on resonant sawtooth
// TB-303 style: each Bass rule carries its own filter envelope
// The filter opens on each note then closes (per-note, per-rule)

@core
@controls
@alphabet.western:browser
@mm:138

cv envSnap : mod.adsr(attack:5, decay:120, sustain:0.15, release:300)
cv envOpen : mod.adsr(attack:5, decay:250, sustain:0.40, release:400)
cv envPluck : mod.adsr(attack:2, decay:80, sustain:0.10, release:200)

S -> Bass Bass Bass Bass

-----

@mode:random

Bass -> C2 C2 C3 C2 - C2 Eb2 C2 (cutoff: envSnap, wave:sawtooth, vel:100, filterQ:8) [weight:50]
Bass -> C2 - Eb2 F2 F#2 F2 Eb2 - (cutoff: envOpen, wave:sawtooth, vel:100, filterQ:8) [weight:30]
Bass -> C2 C2 C2 - G2 - Eb2 C2 (cutoff: envPluck, wave:sawtooth, vel:100, filterQ:8)
